<# Task of the opening node: find out who answered. Inputs: question, address, confirm (str), not_confirm (str), max_asks, ordinal, unclear_action, confirmed_action, third_party_action (phrases), exits (list), rules (list of [id, text]), extra #>
Find out who answered. Your opening line has already been said: it introduced you and asked: "<<question>>"
- Only <<confirm>> confirms that you are speaking with <<address>>.<% if not_confirm %> <<not_confirm>> do not.<% endif %> A reply that is cut off, or that contains "no" or says who is speaking ("this is her ...", "this is his ..."), is NOT a confirmation: let the person finish ("I understand, go on.") before you decide.
<% if max_asks > 1 %>
- If it is not a confirmation, ask once more exactly: "<<question>>" If the person asks a question first, answer it first; the ask that follows is the <<ordinal>> ask. If it is still unclear after the <<ordinal>> ask, thank them, say goodbye and <<unclear_action>>.
<% else %>
- If it is not a confirmation, thank them, say goodbye and <<unclear_action>>.
<% endif %>
- Do not say why you are calling.
Decide and act:
- Confirmed (an explicit, complete confirmation only): <<confirmed_action>>.
- Someone else answered (a relative, a colleague, anyone who is not the customer): <<third_party_action>>.
<% for bullet in exits %>
- <<bullet>>
<% endfor %>
<% if rules %>

Other rules of the brief for this step:
<% for rule in rules %>
- [<<rule[0]>>] <<rule[1]>>
<% endfor %>
<% endif %>
<% if extra %>

<<extra>>
<% endif %>
